course: dictionary
lesson: 12857
title: Formal words that cause feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Engender is a formal word. It means to cause something, or to make it begin, and it is most often used with feelings and attitudes. «Kindness engenders trust» means that kindness makes people trust you.
explain: Read the words around it to find the clues. «The surprise ending engendered a lot of excitement in the class.» The word excitement tells you what was caused, so engendered must mean caused or created.
explain: Check by swapping in a simpler word. «Kindness causes trust» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Engender is a fancier word, so writers use it in essays and reports to sound more precise.
fact: Engender means to cause or create something, often a feeling or an attitude.
fact: Engender is a verb, so its forms are engenders, engendered and engendering.
fact: Useful phrases include «engender trust», «engender fear» and «engender respect».
fact: Engender is a formal word, so you will meet it more in writing than in everyday talk.
fact: An old book may use engender to mean to father a child. This old sense is rare, so you will hardly ever meet it today.
exercise: «Her kind words engendered trust in the new girl.» What does engendered mean here? | Shouted loudly | Measured carefully | Lost or forgotten | *Caused or created
exercise: «Hard practice engenders confidence.» What does engenders mean? | Hides | Measures | Stops | *Causes or creates
exercise: «Good teachers engender a love of reading.» Which word is the closest synonym for engender here? | Break | Measure | Ignore | *Create
test: «The new rules engendered fear among the workers.» What does engendered mean? | *Caused | Removed | Read aloud | Measured
test: Which word is a formal word for cause? | Wobble | *Engender | Happen | Snore
exam: Which sentence uses engender correctly? | The dog engendered the ball across the park. | *A fair leader engenders trust in her team. | I engendered my dinner in the oven. | The sky engendered a bus at noon.
